  "placement": "Book page 37, topic 2.2: সরল স্পন্দন গতি (Simple Harmonic Motion). Next to চিত্র ২.০২ (দোলনা), or in place of it.",
  "order": 2,
  "maintainers": ["RadeenXALNW"],
  "units": "m",
  "description": "Interactive 3D figure for simple harmonic motion (সরল স্পন্দন গতি), book page 37, topic 2.2, next to চিত্র ২.০২ (দোলনা). A girl on a swing hung from a bamboo frame in a village courtyard, a blue tin house behind (or, as a second example, a 2 kg mass on a spring on a lab bench before a blackboard), oscillates about the equilibrium point (সাম্যবিন্দু): a gold, dark-outlined arrow shows the speed, zero at the ends (প্রান্ত) and greatest at the equilibrium point, and cyan dots on the path mark where it is every T/16, close together near the ends and far apart in the middle. The panel shows the speed in m/s and a graph of the speed over one period (পর্যায়কাল). The student pulls the seat (or a rope, or the mass) to one side and lets go, which sets the amplitude; pause, step, or slow time 4x. Physics: x = A cos ωt. Swing: ropes 1.7 m to the seat, L = 1.5 m to the centre of mass of girl and seat, T = 2π√(L/g) = 2.46 s (small-swing formula, kept within 25°, where it is good to 1.3 %). Spring: m = 2 kg, k = 50 N/m, T = 1.26 s. Test tab: 5 questions (where the speed is greatest or zero, how it changes along a marked part of the path, which journey takes one period, the period from a half-swing time, everyday examples). Phone-first, Bangla.",
